# What the nightly `restic backup --tag home` of all of ~ leaves out.
# restic expands ${BACKUP_SOURCE_HOME}. Each comment line gives the reason for
# the patterns under it; scripts/__backup_coverage.sh reports that reason.
# Everything not listed here is backed up, so a new folder in ~ is covered by
# default. The run also skips any single file over 1G (the 4TB drive takes those
# from 17 Nov).

